    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>0</x>
      <y>260</y>
      <w>680</w>
      <h>230</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>We might want to support both of the two functions below,
- Automtical recovery: Disable this feature by default?
- Provide an interrface to let human operators manually trigger the recovery process,
  and optionally Let them to specify which member to recovery from (or recover from a snapshot)?

We can record the following status for users reference, but the controller shouldn't depend
on them to make decision, instead it gets the status from live environment.
- LastRecoveryTime
- RecoveryCount
- LastReveredFrom  

We don't need to add other members into the cluster. Instead, we use the existing scale in/out
process to take care of it.
bg=blue</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
